    "declarations": "Manual pixel-space observations on this exact retained original. The mandible joint owns the coiled proboscis at the true mouth (the template mouthpart actuator; butterflies have no chewing jaws and none was invented). Wings are closed: both visible wing surfaces (near forewing + near hindwing) are owned by wingNear; the far wings are directly behind them and own no paint.",
